.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt RSA_PRINT 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm RSA_print ,
.Nm RSA_print_fp ,
.Nm DSAparams_print ,
.Nm DSAparams_print_fp ,
.Nm DSA_print ,
.Nm DSA_print_fp ,
.Nm DHparams_print ,
.Nm DHparams_print_fp
.Nd print cryptographic parameters
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/rsa.h
The following functions have been deprecated since OpenSSL 3.0, and can
be hidden entirely by defining
.Ar OPENSSL_API_COMPAT
with a suitable version value, see
.Xr openssl_user_macros 7 :
.Ft int
.Fo RSA_print
.Fa "BIO *bp"
.Fa "const RSA *x"
.Fa "int offset"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo RSA_print_fp
.Fa "FILE *fp"
.Fa "const RSA *x"
.Fa "int offset"
.Fc
.In openssl/dsa.h
.Pp
The following functions have been deprecated since OpenSSL 3.0, and can
be hidden entirely by defining
.Ar OPENSSL_API_COMPAT
with a suitable version value, see
.Xr openssl_user_macros 7 :
.Ft int
.Fo DSAparams_print
.Fa "BIO *bp"
.Fa "const DSA *x"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo DSAparams_print_fp
.Fa "FILE *fp"
.Fa "const DSA *x"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo DSA_print
.Fa "BIO *bp"
.Fa "const DSA *x"
.Fa "int offset"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo DSA_print_fp
.Fa "FILE *fp"
.Fa "const DSA *x"
.Fa "int offset"
.Fc
.In openssl/dh.h
.Pp
The following functions have been deprecated since OpenSSL 3.0, and can
be hidden entirely by defining
.Ar OPENSSL_API_COMPAT
with a suitable version value, see
.Xr openssl_user_macros 7 :
.Ft int
.Fo DHparams_print
.Fa "BIO *bp"
.Fa "DH *x"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo DHparams_print_fp
.Fa "FILE *fp"
.Fa "const DH *x"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
All of the functions described on this page are deprecated.
Applications should instead use
.Xr EVP_PKEY_print_params 3
and
.Xr EVP_PKEY_print_private 3 .
.Pp
A human-readable hexadecimal output of the components of the RSA key,
DSA parameters or key or DH parameters is printed to
.Fa bp
or
.Fa fp .
.Pp
The output lines are indented by
.Fa offset
spaces.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn DSAparams_print ,
.Fn DSAparams_print_fp ,
.Fn DSA_print ,
and
.Fn DSA_print_fp
return 1 for success and 0 or a negative value for failure.
.Pp
.Fn DHparams_print
and
.Fn DHparams_print_fp
return 1 on success, 0 on error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Bd -literal
 L<EVP_PKEY_print_params(3)>,
 L<EVP_PKEY_print_private(3)>,
 L<BN_bn2bin(3)>
.Ed
.Sh HISTORY
All of these functions were deprecated in OpenSSL 3.0.
